# NarratIQ AI — Environment Variables
#
# Copy to backend/.env:   cp .env.example backend/.env
#
# On RunPod you normally need NONE of this: start-narratiq.sh generates
# backend/.env for you. See docs/RUNPOD_ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLE_RECOVERY.md.
#
# IMPORTANT: Never commit the real .env file. This example file is safe to commit.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING KEYS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# backend/config.py uses pydantic-settings with extra="forbid" (the default).
# A key in backend/.env that is NOT a field on the Settings class raises
# ValidationError at import and the backend WILL NOT START:
#
#     ValidationError: 1 validation error for Settings
#     <your_key>
#       Extra inputs are not permitted [type=extra_forbidden, ...]
#
# Only keys with a NON-EMPTY value trigger this. Empty keys (FOO=) are ignored.
# Every valid key is a field in backend/config.py — check there before adding.
#
# (This is why TROCR_MODEL_ID was removed from this file: it survived the
#  TrOCR -> GOT-OCR2.0 migration and crashed any backend that copied this file.)
#
# NOTE: HF_TOKEN is NOT a Settings field. It is read only by
# scripts/download_models.sh. Keep it in your SHELL or the RunPod UI, not here.
#
# PRECEDENCE: OS environment variables OVERRIDE this file.
#     env vars  >  backend/.env  >  defaults in config.py
# A stale value in the RunPod UI silently beats whatever is written here.
#
# LOCATION: config.py reads "./.env" relative to the CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY.
# Always start the backend from the backend/ directory, or this file is ignored.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── Security — THE ONLY REQUIRED SETTING ─────────────────────────────────────
# No default. The backend refuses to start without it, and a validator rejects
# anything shorter than 32 characters.
# Generate with: python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
#
# start-narratiq.sh generates this automatically if backend/.env lacks it.
# Set it explicitly (here or in the RunPod UI) to keep existing logins working
# across a fresh clone — changing it invalidates all active JWT sessions.
SECRET_KEY=replace_me_with_64_hex_chars


# ── Database — PostgreSQL 16 + pgvector REQUIRED ─────────────────────────────
# SQLite is NOT supported. The app uses pgvector HNSW indexes and the <=> cosine
# operator; a startup self-check in main.py raises RuntimeError on SQLite.
#
# start-narratiq.sh creates the role/database and FORCE-OVERWRITES this value in
# backend/.env on every run, so you do not need to set it for the scripted path.
# It is left uncommented here so that copying this file also works for a MANUAL
# backend run — without it, config.py falls back to its SQLite default and the
# pgvector startup self-check fails with a confusing error.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://narratiq:narratiq@localhost:5432/narratiq


# ── vLLM server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LEAVE THESE COMMENTED OUT.
#
# start-narratiq.sh launches vLLM on port 9001 and FORCE-OVERWRITES both values
# in backend/.env on every run. config.py already defaults to 9001.
#
# WARNING: the legacy start.sh and scripts/verify_runpod_setup.sh still use port
# 8001. Setting VLLM_BASE_URL to 8001 here — or leaving it set in the RunPod UI
# from an older deployment — points the backend at a dead port. The backend still
# starts (it degrades rather than failing), so the only symptom is that every AI
# feature returns 503 and /api/health reports "vllm": "unavailable".
# See docs/RUNPOD_ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLE_RECOVERY.md §10.
# VLLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9001/v1
# VLLM_MODEL_NAME=Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct


# ── Model directory ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All model subdirectories live under this path.
#   RunPod ephemeral : /workspace/models        (re-downloaded each new pod)
#   RunPod volume    : /runpod-volume/models    (persists)
#
# CAVEAT: start-narratiq.sh hardcodes /workspace/models and exports it, so this
# value is overridden when using that script. For a Network Volume, symlink:
#   ln -s /runpod-volume/models /workspace/models
MODEL_BASE_DIR=/workspace/models

# Optional direct path overrides. Leave empty to derive from MODEL_BASE_DIR.
# LLM_MODEL_PATH=
# BGE_MODEL_PATH=


# ── Hugging Face model IDs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by scripts/download_models.sh. Change only for fine-tuned forks.
# LLM_MODEL_ID=Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct
# BGE_MODEL_ID=BAAI/bge-m3
# GOT_OCR_MODEL_ID=stepfun-ai/GOT-OCR2_0
# WHISPER_MODEL_ID=deepdml/faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo-ct2


# ── GPU / vLLM launch tuning ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LEAVE COMMENTED OUT. start-narratiq.sh auto-detects from GPU count and passes
# CLI flags directly to vLLM — it never reads these. They exist for the legacy
# start.sh and for manual vLLM invocations.
#
#   1 GPU  -> TP=1, GPU_UTIL=0.88, MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192
#   2 GPUs -> TP=2, GPU_UTIL=0.90, MAX_MODEL_LEN=16384
#   4 GPUs -> TP=4, GPU_UTIL=0.90, MAX_MODEL_LEN=32768
#
# Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct has 4 KV heads: TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE must divide 4.
# Valid: 1, 2, 4. NOT 3.
# GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.88
# TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE=1
# MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192


# ── Inference device settings ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "cpu" is the safe default. Use "cuda" only with VRAM headroom above
# GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION.
# BGE_DEVICE=cpu                 # BGE-M3 embeddings: 80-150 ms/query on CPU
# WHISPER_DEVICE=cpu             # faster-whisper transcription
# WHISPER_COMPUTE_TYPE=int8      # int8 for CPU, float16 for GPU


# ── FastAPI server ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# start-narratiq.sh passes --host/--port as CLI flags; these are for manual runs.
# BACKEND_HOST=0.0.0.0
# BACKEND_PORT=8000


# ── CORS origins (JSON list) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# start-narratiq.sh FORCE-OVERWRITES this from the live RUNPOD_POD_ID each run,
# and main.py already allows https://*.proxy.runpod.net via regex.
# Leave commented. A stale pod ID here causes CORS failures.
# CORS_ORIGINS=["http://localhost:3000","http://127.0.0.1:3000"]


# ── JWT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# JWT_EXPIRE_MINUTES=10080       # 7 days. Set 60 in production.
# JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256


# ── Logging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO                 # DEBUG | INFO | WARNING | ERROR | CRITICAL
# LOG_FORMAT=text                # text for dev, json for log aggregators


# ── Rate limiting (slowapi format: "N/period") ───────────────────────────────
# In-memory only. NOTE: SLOWAPI_STORAGE_URI is referenced in some older docs but
# is NOT read by any code — middleware/rate_limit.py builds the Limiter with no
# storage argument. Moving to Redis requires a code change.
# RATE_LIMIT_AUTH=5/minute            # per IP
# RATE_LIMIT_REALTIME_AI=20/minute    # per user
# RATE_LIMIT_HEAVY_AI=5/minute        # per user
# RATE_LIMIT_BACKGROUND_AI=3/minute   # per user
# RATE_LIMIT_UPLOAD=10/minute         # per user
# RATE_LIMIT_VOICE=30/minute          # per user


# ── Upload limits and storage ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MAX_AUDIO_UPLOAD_MB=100
# MAX_OCR_UPLOAD_MB=50
# MAX_MANUSCRIPT_UPLOAD_MB=25
# UPLOAD_DIR_AUDIO=uploads/audio
# UPLOAD_DIR_OCR=uploads/ocr


# ── Background AI concurrency ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BG_AI_CONCURRENCY=3            # max concurrent Qwen background tasks
# EMBEDDING_CONCURRENCY=2        # max concurrent BGE-M3 background tasks


# ── Real-time voice agent ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Master kill-switch. False => voice endpoints return disabled responses and the
# frontend hides the panel.
# VOICE_AGENT_ENABLED=true
#
# Streaming STT (runs on CPU so it never contends with vLLM for VRAM)
# STT_CONCURRENCY=2
# STT_PARTIAL_MODEL=base         # tiny | base | small — read by start-narratiq.sh
# STT_PARTIAL_COMPUTE=int8
#
# Live voice commands are pinned to one language so noisy or accented speech is
# never auto-detected as another language. The legacy upload path still
# auto-detects regardless of this setting.
# VOICE_STT_LANGUAGE=en
# VOICE_STT_AUTO_LANGUAGE=false
# VOICE_NO_SPEECH_THRESHOLD=0.6
# VOICE_LOGPROB_THRESHOLD=-1.0
# VOICE_MIN_PARTIAL_CHARS=2
# VOICE_MIN_FINAL_CONFIDENCE=0.0
# VOICE_VOCAB_FUZZY_MIN=84
# VOICE_VOCAB_ENABLED=true
#
# Behaviour limits
# MAX_VOICE_AUDIO_MB=25
# VOICE_SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES=30
# VOICE_MAX_GRAPH_NODES=8
# VOICE_INTENT_SHORTLIST_K=8
# VOICE_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.55
# VOICE_LOW_CONFIDENCE_FLOOR=0.35
# VOICE_ADMIN_EMAILS=[]          # JSON list; may read /api/voice/analytics/*


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT SETTINGS FIELDS — do not put these in backend/.env
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HF_TOKEN            Read only by scripts/download_models.sh. Export in the
#                     shell or set in the RunPod UI:
#                         export HF_TOKEN=hf_your_token_here
#                     Optional: Qwen2.5-7B, BGE-M3 and GOT-OCR2.0 are public.
#
# RUNPOD_POD_ID       Injected by RunPod. Read by start-narratiq.sh to build the
#                     public proxy URLs. Never set by hand.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL Frontend only. Written to frontend/.env.local by
#                     start-narratiq.sh and inlined at BUILD time. Changing it
#                     requires a rebuild, not a restart.
#
# SLOWAPI_STORAGE_URI Referenced in older docs but never read by any code.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
